course: dictionary
lesson: 11836
title: Blazing: bright, hot, angry or fast
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Blazing comes from the word blaze, which means a bright, strong fire or light. «The blazing fire kept us warm all evening.» A fire that is blazing is burning brightly and strongly, so the words around blazing tell you what it means.
explain: The same word can describe heat and light too. «Wear sun cream on a blazing hot day.» Here blazing means very hot or very bright. Look at what it describes: a fire, a sun, a day. The thing it describes is your first clue.
explain: In informal talk, blazing can mean very angry or very fast. «They had a blazing row about the football.» A row is an argument, so a blazing row is a very loud, angry one. Another example is «The runner set off at blazing speed.» Check each meaning by swapping it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Blazing is an adjective, and it comes from the verb blaze.
fact: «Blazing» means burning brightly and strongly, like a fire.
fact: «Blazing» means very hot or very bright, as in «blazing sun».
fact: «Blazing» can mean very angry in informal talk, as in «a blazing row».
fact: «Blazing» can also mean very fast, as in «at blazing speed».
exercise: «The house was blazing when the firefighters arrived.» What does blazing mean here? | Cold and empty | Very quiet and still | Painted in bright colours | *Burning brightly and strongly
exercise: «Wear sun cream on a blazing hot day.» What does blazing mean here? | *Very hot or very bright | Very soft | Very wet and cold | Very slow
exercise: Mia says, «They had a blazing row, and everyone heard it.» What does blazing row mean? | A race run at speed | *A very angry, loud argument | A long, quiet walk | A bright show of fireworks
test: «The runner shot off at blazing speed.» What does blazing mean here? | Very slow | Very quiet | Very cold | *Very fast
test: «The campfire was blazing, so we stayed close to it for warmth.» What is the best meaning? | *Burning brightly and strongly | Dark and damp | Very quiet | Frozen solid
exam: Which sentence uses blazing to mean very angry? | We ran at blazing speed | The blazing fire kept us warm | *They had a blazing row in the kitchen | The blazing sun rose over the hill
